%% encyclopedia.sty -- the functionality names that belong to the encyclopedia
%% and not to the book.
%%
%% Split out of ucgamers.sty on 18 August 2026, for one reason: ucgamers.sty is
%% a genuine input of *UC for Gamers*, watched by scripts/artifact_manifest.py,
%% so editing it marks the committed PDF and the HTML edition stale and asks
%% for `pdflatex main.tex` plus the four-minute scripts/build_uc_html.sh. That
%% is right for a change to the book's notation and wrong for the one
%% \newcommand every new encyclopedia entry needs: main.tex never \inputs those
%% fragments, so it never expands those macros, and a rebuild changes nothing
%% but the \today on the title page. Ninety-odd entries remain to be written;
%% this file is what keeps each of them from being a book event.
%%
%% The rule for which file a macro goes in is therefore about the book, not
%% about the notation: if any box main.tex \inputs can mention it, it belongs
%% in ucgamers.sty; if only an encyclopedia-only fragment can, it belongs here.
%% Nothing here may be needed to *typeset* a box -- the environments, the
%% palette and the shared notation all stay in ucgamers.sty, which this file
%% assumes has already been loaded.
%%
%% Read by three consumers, none of which is main.tex:
%%   * scripts/gen_interface.py (load_macros), which renders the fragments to
%%     their uc/.../index.qmd pages -- and whose MACRO_OVERRIDES still applies,
%%     so a macro added here whose expansion is not valid MathJax needs an
%%     entry there just as it would in ucgamers.sty;
%%   * scripts/build_uc_html.sh, through that same loader, to feed MathJax;
%%   * functionalities/preview.tex, which compiles one fragment standalone.
%%
%% preview.tex \inputs this file rather than \usepackage'ing it, since it
%% sits in functionalities/ rather than on TeX's search path -- which is the
%% point: keeping it out of latex/ is what keeps it out of the glob in
%% artifact_manifest.py's book_inputs().
%%
%% Names are kept in the book's own casing, so a box promoted into a later
%% chapter needs no renaming -- only its \newcommand moved back across.
\ProvidesFile{functionalities/encyclopedia.sty}[2026/08/18 encyclopedia-only functionality names]

